\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces Illustration of the BO molecular potential curves (solid thick lines) participating in the radiative association process. In the $ A^2\Sigma ^+ $ entrance channel, the wave function is shown by the light undulating line. The oscillations are due to the strong polarization force in the entrance channel, leading to a potential minimum at $ R \approx 14a_0 $. Association is precipitated by the emission of a photon of energy $ \omega $ near the classical turning point. The final bound rho-vibrational state, in the $ X^2\Sigma ^+ $ channel, is shown by the thin line.}}{15}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{RadAssoc4}{{2.1}{15}{Illustration of the BO molecular potential curves (solid thick lines) participating in the radiative association process. In the $ A^2\Sigma ^+ $ entrance channel, the wave function is shown by the light undulating line. The oscillations are due to the strong polarization force in the entrance channel, leading to a potential minimum at $ R \approx 14a_0 $. Association is precipitated by the emission of a photon of energy $ \omega $ near the classical turning point. The final bound rho-vibrational state, in the $ X^2\Sigma ^+ $ channel, is shown by the thin line}{figure.caption.8}{}}
